 ('EPM-00953-A','REF-00953','REF-00953','MOB','19 residential aged-care residents (6M/13F) plus 5 staff and 2 clinicians, Queensland Australia; selected BY facility staff, researchers not permitted to approach residents directly',19,
  'PARTIAL','Study population is institutional aged-care residents, not disabled people as such, so PARTIAL not EXACT. It is closer than a general older cohort because the observed task - sit-to-stand transfer - IS the served demand. Two caveats recorded rather than smoothed: facility-gatekept selection, and the authors note the sample is not representative of aged care generally in anthropometrics, abilities or attitudes.',NULL,'2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b2'),
 ('EPM-00955-A','REF-00955','REF-00955','DEM','25 people living with dementia, Metro Vancouver',25,
  'PARTIAL','Population of study is people living with dementia; the bench finding is about sustained-exertion demand, which this cohort has alongside orientation demand. PARTIAL - the association is credible for the served demand but was not measured on it in isolation.',NULL,'2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b2'),
 ('EPM-00956-A','REF-00956','REF-00956','MOB','525 community-dwelling seniors, Czech Republic, urban and rural',525,
  'PROXY','General senior population, not selected for disability or mobility limitation. PROXY. The finding used from this source is DISTRIBUTIONAL (rural areas have substantially worse bench availability), which transfers across populations more readily than an effect estimate would.',NULL,'2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b2'),
 ('EPM-00957-A','REF-00957','REF-00957','MOB','Modelled profiles, not enrolled participants: three older-adult profiles including one with reduced mobility, two suburban Grenoble neighbourhoods',NULL,
  'PROXY','No participants - a spatial model. Graded PROXY per the rule that a source with no participants is PROXY at best. It does explicitly model "an older adult with reduced mobility", so the served demand is represented in the model even though nobody was studied.',NULL,'2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b2'),
 ('EPM-00958-A','REF-00958','REF-00958','MOB','38 older adults (19 women), mean age 72.8 (SD 7.4), Hong Kong; 47% recruited from private elderly centres',38,
  'PROXY','General older-adult cohort not selected for disability. PROXY. Value is corroborative and geographic (non-Western setting), not parameter-setting.',NULL,'2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b2'),
 ('EPM-00959-A','REF-00959','REF-00959','ALL','3,677 across four age groups (758 children, 897 adolescents, 1,655 younger adults, 367 older adults), US multicenter',3677,
  'PROXY','General-population instrument-validation sample spanning children to older adults, NOT a disabled cohort - PROXY per the rule that general-population and child samples are PROXY. Target recorded as ALL rather than a specific code because the instrument is population-agnostic. Its evidential weight here is that benches survived empirical item selection, not that it measures the served population.',NULL,'2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b2');

